{"hsID": "73739951432", "pin": "82266", "category": "Exhibitor", "confirmed": "1", "optin_delegate": "1", "reference": "11373", "aboutMe": "Veer Ahuja is the Director of Solution Architecture for ETP Group’s cloud-native Unified Commerce Solutions.

With a Master's Degree in Economics and Business Management from Heriot-Watt University in Edinburgh, UK and 10 years of experience in retail, omni-channel and e-commerce technology, Veer has spent time across all departments in ETP, focusing heavily on R&amp;D, Consulting, and Solutioning. Veer is keenly interested in the evolution of e-commerce and physical retail, and the convergence of these into a cohesive experience for consumers. He sees this being done through new cutting-edge technology, and is keen to witness and experience how retailers, manufacturers and distributors around the world adapt to it to create a seamless customer experience.

When he isn't working on digital transformation, he enjoys scuba diving, playing football, watching MMA, keeping fit, and spending time with his family and his dog.", "updated": "2026-06-03 04:11:52"}

{"hsID": "220153493263", "pin": "89719", "category": "Delegate (Retailer)", "confirmed": "1", "optin_delegate": "1", "reference": "12620", "aboutMe": "I’m the Head of End User Operations at Foodstuffs South Island, leading customer support, service operations, and modern workplace technology across one of New Zealand’s largest retail networks. I have over 6 years’ experience in the health industry and more than 5 years with Foodstuffs South Island, bringing a strong people-focused and operational approach to technology leadership.

I’ve helped lead our ServiceNow transformation journey, driving service management maturity, automation, and improved end-user experiences across the business. My portfolio includes Microsoft collaboration and audio solutions, voice services, digital signage, endpoint management, and retail support operations across supermarkets, distribution centres, and support offices.

I’m passionate about AI, innovation, retail technology, and service transformation, with a strong focus on practical technology outcomes that support frontline teams and improve operational efficiency.", "updated": "2026-06-03 04:12:11"}

{"hsID": "224671387495", "pin": "12747", "category": "Exhibitor", "confirmed": "1", "optin_delegate": "1", "reference": "17351", "aboutMe": "As Director of Partnerships for Retail Media at Broadsign, I lead our global strategy to build a connected ecosystem of partners shaping the future of in-store retail media. My mission is to bring together technology providers, integrators, and data partners to create seamless, scalable, and measurable in-store media experiences for retailers and brands worldwide.

With a focus on collaboration and commercial growth, I work at the intersection of digital signage, ad tech, and retail innovation — developing partnerships that enhance Broadsign’s offering, enable new monetisation models, and deliver tangible value to both our customers and their shoppers.

Driven by curiosity and a belief in open ecosystems, I’m passionate about transforming physical retail spaces into smarter, more engaging environments through technology, creativity, and meaningful partnerships.", "updated": "2026-06-03 04:13:33"}

